#
# mdwfTwoPlusOneHmcRun.param -- 2+1 flavour Mobius domain-wall HMC (main_mdwfTwoPlusOneHmcRun.cpp)
#
# This example: the DSDR production setup on a small lattice (8^4, Ls = 8, a few minutes on one GPU):
# Iwasaki gauge action, even/odd preconditioning, c_sw = 0, light quark pair with one Hasenbusch mass,
# DSDR weight, exact one-flavour (EOFA) strange quark, mixed-precision solvers, antiperiodic fermions in time.
#
#   ./mdwfTwoPlusOneHmcRun ../parameter/tests/mdwfTwoPlusOneHmcRun.param [key=value ...]
#
# Each trajectory appends one line to <measurements_dir>/<output_name>:
#   traj accepted deltaH exp(-deltaH) plaquette kinetic_before gauge_before fermion_before fermion_forces seconds
#
# Lattice
#            Lattice: Nx Ny Nz Nt
#              Nodes: ranks per direction (more than one rank needs c_sw = 0)
# Gauge action (default: Wilson plaquette)
#    rectangle_gauge: 1 = plaquette + rectangle, S_g = -(beta/3) [(1 - 8 c1) sum Re tr U_p + c1 sum Re tr U_rect]
#           gauge_c1: rectangle coefficient c1 (Iwasaki -0.331, DBW2 -1.4088)
#     symanzik_gauge: 1 = tree-level Symanzik instead (not together with rectangle_gauge)
# Fermions
#     antiperiodic_t: fermion boundary condition in time (1 = antiperiodic, needed at finite temperature)
#           even_odd: 1 = even/odd preconditioned actions (needed for Hasenbusch, DSDR, EOFA), 0 = M^+ M
#                 Ls: 8, or 16 together with dsdr_twists
#   M5, b5, c_sw: Mobius kernel D_W(-M5), c5 = b5 - 1; c_sw = 0 for the even/odd light form used here
#             mf, ms: light and strange quark mass;  pv_mass: Pauli-Villars mass (1.0)
#  hasenbusch_masses: intermediate light masses mf < m_1 < ... < pv_mass (empty: one ratio)
#        dsdr_twists: DSDR twists eps_0 < eps_1 < ... (empty: no DSDR); D_W at dsdr_M5 (default: M5)
#       strange_eofa: 1 = EOFA strange quark, det M(ms) / det M(pv_mass) (needs hasenbusch_masses and dsdr_twists);
#                     0 = rational (RHMC) strange quark, see below
#   eofa_lambda_low, eofa_lambda_high: interval of the EOFA heatbath approximation x^(-1/2)
# Molecular dynamics
#                tau: trajectory length (GPT units: tau_GPT = sqrt(2) tau, so 0.70710678 = GPT's tau 1)
#      fermion_steps: steps of the fermion level per trajectory
#     gauge_substeps: gauge steps per fermion step
#          md_scheme: 0 leapfrog, 1 OMF2 (omf2_lambda), 2 OMF2 force-gradient
#   term_level, level_substeps: optional multi-level integrator (one level per fermion force term:
#                     Hasenbusch factors lightest first, strange, then DSDR factors); unset = two levels
# Solvers
#          precision: CG residual of the action and heatbath solves;  force_precision: of the force solves
#    mixed_precision: 1 = single-precision CG with double reliable updates;  chrono_size: number of previous
#                     force solutions used for the initial guess (needs mixed_precision = 1)
#           max_iter: CG iteration limit
# Run control
#             n_traj: trajectories;  n_therm: excluded from the statistics;  n_nometro (<= n_therm): accepted
#                     without Metropolis test;  block_size: block length of the blocked error
#               seed: random number seed
#   check_steps: Lanczos check of the RHMC intervals on the start configuration (0 = off; not used by EOFA)
#   measurements_dir, output_name: per-trajectory output
#      Gaugefile_out: configuration written (NERSC) into measurements_dir every save_every trajectories (0: at
#                     the end only);  Gaugefile: start configuration (unset: cold start)
#        max_seconds: start no trajectory past this wall-clock budget (0: no limit)
#
# Further keys (defaults in brackets): RHMC strange quark (strange_eofa = 0): lambda_low_s [0.04],
# lambda_high_s [180], lambda_low_pv [0.2], lambda_high_pv [180] (intervals of M^+ M or Mhat^+ Mhat, measure them
# with mdwfSpectralBounds), action_error [1e-12], force_error [1e-8], max_order [30], remez_digits [50];
# eofa_error [1e-10], eofa_check_heatbath [1], light_form [1 = GPT form, needs c_sw = 0; 0 = original form],
# mixed_delta [0.1], gauge_scheme [-1 = md_scheme], omf2_lambda [0.18], conf_double [0: 2 rows, single
# precision], traj_offset [0] and save_series [0] (chained segments), reversibility_check [0 = off; n > 0: n
# forward/backward checks instead of the run], force_halos [1].
#
Lattice           = 8 8 8 8
Nodes             = 1 1 1 1
beta              = 1.8
rectangle_gauge   = 1
gauge_c1          = -0.331
antiperiodic_t    = 1
even_odd          = 1
Ls                = 8
M5                = 1.8
b5                = 1.5
c_sw              = 0.0
mf                = 0.05
ms                = 0.1
pv_mass           = 1.0
hasenbusch_masses = 0.3
dsdr_twists       = 0.02 0.07 0.18 0.5
strange_eofa      = 1
eofa_lambda_low   = 1.0
eofa_lambda_high  = 12.0
tau               = 0.70710678
fermion_steps     = 6
gauge_substeps    = 4
md_scheme         = 2
precision         = 1e-10
force_precision   = 1e-8
mixed_precision   = 1
chrono_size       = 6
max_iter          = 100000
n_traj            = 10
n_therm           = 5
n_nometro         = 2
block_size        = 1
seed              = 20261023
check_steps       = 0
save_every        = 0
max_seconds       = 0
measurements_dir  = ./
output_name       = mdwfTwoPlusOneHmcRun.dat
Gaugefile_out     = mdwfTwoPlusOneHmcRun.nersc
#Gaugefile        = /path/to/start.nersc
